32l6|n|To free from accusation, or the imputation of fault or blame; to clear from guilt; to release from a charge; to justify by extenuating a fault; to exculpate; to absolve; to acquit. ; To pardon, as a fault; to forgive entirely, or to admit to be little censurable, and to overlook; as, we excuse irregular conduct, when extraordinary circumstances appear to justify it. ; To regard with indulgence; to view leniently or to overlook; to pardon. ; To free from an impending obligation or duty; hence, to disengage; to dispense with; to release by favor; also, to remit by favor; not to exact; as, to excuse a forfeiture. ; To relieve of an imputation by apology or defense; to make apology for as not seriously evil; to ask pardon or indulgence for. ; The act of excusing, apologizing, exculpating, pardoning, releasing, and the like; acquittal; release; absolution; justification; extenuation. ; That which is offered as a reason for being excused; a plea offered in extenuation of a fault or irregular deportment; apology; as, an excuse for neglect of duty; excuses for delay of payment. ; That which excuses; that which extenuates or justifies a fault.	a:53eu,106,9;9a9d,101,3;3clz,81,34;15q7,61,8;5uwt,58,12;79k7,47,237;8rmn,43,9;7ru5,39,198;77gx,29,15;3sqe,26,1116;70tt,26,108;770l,25,1;77r8,22,6;9lm9,21,20;328g,20,35~3sqe,26,1116;79k7,47,237;7ru5,39,198;3ugs,14,135;70tt,26,108;5b7l,3,83;328g,20,35;3clz,81,34;1fqp,20,23;9lm9,21,20;amke,17,19;77gx,29,15;5uwt,58,12;a86l,15,12;53eu,106,9	v:77gx,10,4~77gx,10,4	V:3f4q,8,15~3f4q,8,15	n:3clz,65,11;77gx,34,21;77r8,30,11;a00p,28,2;14k9,26,12;9zwe,19,4;56li,19,3;al68,6,272;6l4j,2,23;9yr5,2,1~al68,6,272;6l4j,2,23;77gx,34,21;14k9,26,12;77r8,30,11;3clz,65,11;9zwe,19,4;56li,19,3;a00p,28,2;9yr5,2,1	N:9y1j,47,28;8gob,39,3;aitb,24,8;1p2r,22,7;7jno,13,2;6mtd,4,1~9y1j,47,28;aitb,24,8;1p2r,22,7;8gob,39,3;7jno,13,2;6mtd,4,1
