33to|n|To become suddenly expanded into a great volume of gas or vapor; to burst violently into flame; as gunpowder explodes. ; To burst with force and a loud report; to detonate, as a shell filled with powder or the like material, or as a boiler from too great pressure of steam. ; To burst forth with sudden violence and noise; as, at this, his wrath exploded. ; To drive from the stage by noisy expressions of disapprobation; to hoot off; to drive away or reject noisily; as, to explode a play. ; To bring into disrepute, and reject; to drive from notice and acceptance; as, to explode a scheme, fashion, or doctrine. ; To cause to explode or burst noisily; to detonate; as, to explode powder by touching it with fire. ; To drive out with violence and noise, as by powder.	a:99m2,71,13;99m1,55,11;73yv,50,2;10zu,49,14;3mor,49,8;9pap,38,2;6h6e,30,3;97s7,26,5;3sp6,20,16;7ni3,16,66;4dn9,10,2;73vx,4,86;10yl,0,1~73vx,4,86;7ni3,16,66;3sp6,20,16;10zu,49,14;99m2,71,13;99m1,55,11;3mor,49,8;97s7,26,5;6h6e,30,3;73yv,50,2;4dn9,10,2;9pap,38,2;10yl,0,1	v:8wy1,42,2;1sku,31,3;8y6p,28,3;120k,18,3;4dn9,10,2;a7g2,2,746~a7g2,2,746;120k,18,3;8y6p,28,3;1sku,31,3;8wy1,42,2;4dn9,10,2	V:8y06,35,22;46lu,27,1;33tv,15,1;61rk,4,1;33j2,3,5~8y06,35,22;33j2,3,5;46lu,27,1;61rk,4,1;33tv,15,1	n:73yv,73,10;10yl,48,28;4dn9,38,14;99m2,34,1;10zu,31,4;12u5,30,37;73vx,29,484;9pap,28,1;40ht,21,137;5v92,14,1;120k,2,1;40pc,0,4~73vx,29,484;40ht,21,137;12u5,30,37;10yl,48,28;4dn9,38,14;73yv,73,10;40pc,0,4;10zu,31,4;5v92,14,1;99m2,34,1;120k,2,1;9pap,28,1	N:9ylh,111,4;46lu,47,4;94wr,40,1;am3p,39,1;4dn9,39,15;61rk,37,10;2ak7,34,1;6sag,25,4;59sw,15,145;3iqq,13,937;8y06,13,5;2aks,13,8;2ruo,6,49;97s7,3,1~3iqq,13,937;59sw,15,145;2ruo,6,49;4dn9,39,15;61rk,37,10;2aks,13,8;8y06,13,5;9ylh,111,4;6sag,25,4;46lu,47,4;2ak7,34,1;am3p,39,1;97s7,3,1;94wr,40,1
