34kc|n|That which is extracted or drawn out. ; A portion of a book or document, separately transcribed; a citation; a quotation. ; A decoction, solution, or infusion made by drawing out from any substance that which gives it its essential and characteristic virtue; essence; as, extract of beef; extract of dandelion; also, any substance so extracted, and characteristic of that from which it is obtained; as, quinine is the most important extract of Peruvian bark. ; A solid preparation obtained by evaporating a solution of a drug, etc., or the fresh juice of a plant; -- distinguished from an abstract. See Abstract, n., 4. ; A peculiar principle once erroneously supposed to form the basis of all vegetable extracts; -- called also the extractive principle. ; Extraction; descent. ; A draught or copy of writing; certified copy of the proceedings in an action and the judgement therein, with an order for execution.	a:30gi,98,12;6uty,82,3;62si,81,9;7a4n,78,7;1m79,78,4;7kmn,77,4;7bal,76,9;a8c8,73,10;92ea,72,3;5ivw,68,144;6v5c,68,2;a25t,65,1;6fj3,61,1;16ev,61,4;2sxt,60,4~5ivw,68,144;aqzj,25,47;13pe,5,35;5jy4,25,30;a93y,13,27;86of,52,26;45fo,21,23;9ej3,3,17;56sm,21,17;hpe,31,15;3im4,46,15;423x,54,14;1qou,13,14;4gus,45,14;3kmg,22,13	v:a25t,85,4;8eay,39,3;45h1,37,4;3cay,31,3;408o,29,1;6vm6,28,2;9sep,22,157;3cau,21,3;an8,20,3;5ivw,17,4;14v,16,2;129m,12,1;7twj,9,23;28um,5,4;2g5u,5,2~9sep,22,157;7twj,9,23;28um,5,4;45h1,37,4;5ivw,17,4;a25t,85,4;3cau,21,3;3cay,31,3;an8,20,3;8eay,39,3;14v,16,2;2g5u,5,2;6vm6,28,2;129m,12,1;408o,29,1	V:622c,68,4;7pzb,58,1;2m9s,42,3;3cay,41,6;9x1j,37,1;3mes,32,44;a4fn,30,3;atpz,20,11;2e0m,20,2;46g1,17,2;13ip,16,7;97sp,14,45;13ik,13,1;3x7l,13,3;84hf,6,1~2u8d,5,82;97sp,14,45;3mes,32,44;1qb8,2,23;atpz,20,11;13ip,16,7;1ttk,3,6;3cay,41,6;622c,68,4;3x7l,13,3;a4fn,30,3;2m9s,42,3;2e0m,20,2;9cg3,2,2;46g1,17,2	n:3us0,101,42;7kmn,96,15;5ivw,91,684;au85,81,6;6fj3,77,3;7a4n,70,4;6vi4,68,2;92xp,66,13;92ea,66,2;an8,65,68;25mk,64,1;70lf,63,18;6qrn,59,13;a93y,59,650;6v5c,5